{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the swarm was removed from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people, tomorrow</b> (וסר הערב מפרעה מעבדיו ומעמו מחר). Just as Pharaoh said at the plague of the frogs \"tomorrow\" (למחר), so Moses wished to do in this matter as well — to pray and they would depart <b>tomorrow</b> (מחר). But behold, the swarm departed and they went away, not as it was with the frogs, for the reason that our Sages stated (Exodus Rabbah 11:3): the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to distress them through the plagues, not to benefit them at all. And Moses was careful in this regard when he said to Pharaoh \"to cut off the frogs\" (להכרית הצפרדעים), thereby hinting at their death, as I have explained (Ramban on Exodus 8:5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:46.082573502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}